  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Supporting the DESC initiative in Kazakhstan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In response to the challenges imposed by the diverse political, economic, and climate conditions involving the continuous expansion of borders, the IOM has developed the Document Examination Support Center (DESC) &#x2013; an initiative to assist governments through capacity building in travel documents and identity examination and verification. Through this project, and after several presentations conducted by the IOM in 2022, the Government of the Republic of Kazakhstan has provided, in a kind contribution, the willingness to support the launch of the DESC initiative in Kazakhstan at the institutional level. This project, thus, focuses on this foundation for the further development of the Kazakhstan border security and management &#x2013; with the additional aid of the Bureau of International Narcotics and Law Enforcement Affairs at the US Embassy in Astana (INL/US Embassy), the DESC initiative plans to contribute to the strengthening of the authorities&#x2019; network in responses in border control and a tighter, safer and more just maintenance of migration justice.</narrative>
  </description>
